* AD8237 Instrumentation Amplifier, G = +10 (20 dB), Single 5 V Supply
* Differential input: 20 mV amplitude, 1 kHz sine; REF at mid-supply (2.5 V)
*
* Vendor macro-model library
.lib AD8237.lib
*
* ---------------- Supplies ----------------
VCC   VCC   0   DC 5
CBYP  VCC   0   0.1u
*
* Mid-supply reference (ideal 2.5 V buffer)
VREF  REF   0   DC 2.5
*
* ---------------- Signal source ----------------
* Single-ended drive on +IN gives a 20 mV amplitude differential signal
VIN   IN    0   SINE(2.5 20m 1k)
VCM   INN   0   DC 2.5
*
* ---------------- AD8237 ----------------
* Subcircuit pin order: REF  -IN  +IN  -VS  FB  OUT  +VS
XU1   REF  INN  IN  0  FB  OUT  VCC  AD8237
*
* Gain-set feedback network: G = 1 + R2/R1 = 1 + 9k/1k = 10 V/V
R1    FB   REF   1k
R2    OUT  FB    9k
*
* ---------------- Load ----------------
RL    OUT  REF   100k
CL    OUT  0     100p
*
* ---------------- Analysis ----------------
.tran 0 5m 0 1u
*
.meas TRAN vout_pp PP V(OUT) FROM 1m TO 5m
.meas TRAN vin_pp  PP V(IN)  FROM 1m TO 5m
.meas TRAN gain    PARAM vout_pp/vin_pp
.meas TRAN gain_db PARAM 20*log10(vout_pp/vin_pp)
.meas TRAN vout_dc AVG V(OUT) FROM 1m TO 5m
*
.options plotwinsize=0
.end
